<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rao Surjan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1554–1585</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Surjan Singh of Bundi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rao Surjan was the Hada ruler of Bundi who held the great fortress of Ranthambore. Besieged by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akbar">Akbar</a>, he surrendered it in 1569 on favourable terms and entered Mughal service, becoming a respected commander and governor. His submission set the pattern for Bundi's long service in Mughal armies, while rival <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> states such as Mewar continued to resist.</p></div>
